menu "Lichen NVS encryption (#116)"
    config LICHEN_NVS_ENCRYPT
        bool "Keep NVS encrypted once an HMAC key is burned"
        default n
        help
            Compiles the encrypted-NVS boot path. It only ever USES a key: with no HMAC key in the configured eFuse
            block (LICHEN_NVS_HMAC_KEY_ID) NVS stays plain, exactly as with this option off. It never creates or burns a
            key. With a key present, a plaintext NVS is copied to RAM once, the partition is erased and the entries are
            written back encrypted. Do not turn on IDF's CONFIG_NVS_ENCRYPTION instead: its init burns a key by itself.
            Read docs/nvs-encryption.md first.

    config LICHEN_NVS_HMAC_KEY_ID
        int "eFuse key block holding the NVS HMAC key (0..5 = KEY0..KEY5)"
        range 0 5
        default 5
        help
            Last block, so KEY0.. stay free for secure boot or flash encryption later. Set in every build, not only
            with LICHEN_NVS_ENCRYPT: a build without it still reads this block's key purpose (read only) and leaves
            NVS alone when a key is burned, since a plain init would erase an encrypted partition entry by entry.

    config LICHEN_NVS_ENCRYPT_BURN_CMD
        bool "Compile fw nvs-enc burn (IRREVERSIBLE eFuse burn)"
        depends on LICHEN_NVS_ENCRYPT
        default n
        help
            Adds "fw nvs-enc burn YES": writes a random 32-byte key with purpose HMAC_UP into the configured block, read
            and write protected. Irreversible; the key cannot be read back or changed. Leave off in every build that is
            not the one deliberate burn build.

    config LICHEN_NVS_DEBUG_FORCE_DOWN
        bool "Compile fw nvs-down YES (bench only: the next boot leaves NVS down)"
        default n
        help
            Adds "fw nvs-down YES" (USB console only): the next boot takes the burned-key "stays down" path once,
            without initialising or erasing NVS, so the boot without settings and the refused Wi-Fi updates can be
            seen on a badge with no key burned. Nothing is written to flash or eFuse; the boot after is normal again.
endmenu
